Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is where contentstack.Stack() is initialized (line 69). The options object (lines 55-67) lacks the live_preview configuration that the Contentstack SDK requires to enable real-time preview. The SDK's default config (confirmed in node_modules/contentstack/config.js) sets live_preview.enable to false; without explicitly passing live_preview:{enable:true, host:...} in the Stack options, the SDK never enters preview mode and no downstream component can receive live preview data. This is the root cause — every component reads content via useContent→ContentstackContext→Stack, but Stack was never configured for live preview.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST to the env destructuring block (lines 17-24), then add a conditional live_preview entry to the options object immediately after the existing CONTENTSTACK_FETCH_TIMEOUT conditional (after line 66, before the closing };), following the identical pattern: ...(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST ? { live_preview: { enable: true, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST } } : {}). This mirrors the existing conditional fetchOptions pattern and uses the Contentstack SDK's documented live_preview Stack option (confirmed in node_modules/contentstack/index.d.ts: Config.live_preview?: LivePreview where LivePreview = { enable: boolean, host: string, management_token?: string }).


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- The behavior described in the ticket is observed to be correct after the change: "[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS".
- Existing behavior related to this area is unchanged (no regression).

